DeckCraft VAIO preview

Open DeckCraft (VAIO preview) from Office or VAIO App Launcher. Ctrl+O opens,
Ctrl+S saves, and Save As chooses another filename. The native .deckcraft format
keeps the application's model; PPTX exchanges presentations with other tools.
Use the ribbon for slides/layouts, text, shapes, pictures, tables, charts, notes,
review and transitions. Start a slide show with Present; Escape returns to editing.
Presenter View is off initially on this single-screen VAIO; enable it in the
Slide Show controls when needed. Static slides wait for input instead of redrawing
continuously; timed shows and active animations keep their playback scheduling.
While presenting, a worker in DeckCraft sends XScreenSaver an awake reminder every
45 seconds. It stops when the show ends or the process exits. The existing
five-minute screensaver setting is retained and applies normally while editing.
PDF export can produce slides, notes pages or handouts. deckcraft-vaio-cli provides
headless commands; no control or MCP server is enabled by the desktop entry.

The VAIO build selects OpenGL/Glow, fits the screen and defaults to a steady caret.
This removes the repeated idle repaint cost observed with a blinking text caret.
Set DECKCRAFT_STATIC_CARET=0 when launching to restore blinking, with higher CPU use.
Native Save As fills the suggested extension when none is typed, and asks before
replacing a different, existing normalized destination. Explicit extensions stay.

This package retains upstream media codecs and audio support, but audio output
is OFF by default because this VAIO previously stalled its HDA audio playback.
DECKCRAFT_ENABLE_AUDIO=1 deckcraft-vaio opts in for that launch; audio output has
not been validated on this machine. Silent slides and transitions work normally.

The pinned craft-fonts input supplies 48 allowed font faces with their original
OFL notices, including Latin presentation fonts, Japanese and Arabic fallback.
Upstream excludes Adobe-authored families. No proprietary Office fonts are shipped.

Small synthetic decks were checked for editing, PPTX save/reopen, pictures,
charts, notes, PDF/outline export, rendering and full-screen silent presentation.
This is upstream alpha software. Complex external PPTX fidelity, heavy animations,
embedded video, actual audio output, physical printing and second-monitor presenter
placement remain unverified. Keep an original copy when exchanging complex decks.

Updates use the signed APT source and the existing Check & Install Updates tool.
Remove with sudo apt-get remove deckcraft-vaio; user files/settings are retained.
